              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            It is a classical fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+enveloping+algebra"} universal enveloping algebra
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            provides a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+deformation+quantization"} formal deformation quantization
            of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structure"} Lie-Poisson structure
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeformationQuantizationOfLiePoissonStructuresByUniversalEnvelopingAlgebras"}
            below). Remarkably, this statement generalizes to more general polynomial Poisson algebras (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynomialPoissonAlgebra"}
            below) for a suitable generalized concept of universal enveloping algebra (def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeformationQuantizationOfLiePoissonStructuresByUniversalEnvelopingAlgebras"}
            below): it is
            %em always
            true up to third order in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℏ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#PenkavaVanhaecke00"} Penkava-Vanhaecke 00, theorem 3.2
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraProvidesDeformationQuantizationAtLeastToOrder3"}
            below). In particular it also holds true for restrictions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+bracket+Lie+algebras"} Poisson bracket Lie algebras
            to their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebras"} Heisenberg Lie algebras
            (example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DeformationQuantizationOfLiePoissonStructuresByUniversalEnvelopingAlgebras"}
            below).
          %h2#definition Definition
          #PolynomialPoissonAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+algebra"} Poisson algebra
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+algebra"} Poisson algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ((A,\cdot), \{-,-\})
              is called a
              %em polynomial Poisson algebra
              if the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,\cdot)
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+algebra"} polynomial algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+algebra"} symmetric algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Sym(V) \coloneqq T(V)/(x \otimes y - y \otimes x \vert x,y \in V)
            %p
              on some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T(V) \coloneqq \underset{n \in \mathbb{N}}{\oplus} V^{\otimes^n}
            %p
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+algebra"} tensor algebra
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi μ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mu \;\colon\; T(V) \longrightarrow Sym(V)
            %p
              for the canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
              map (which is an algebra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma \;\colon\; Sym(V) \longrightarrow T(V)
            %p
              for its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear
              inverse (symmetrization, which is not in general an algebra
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %p
              Notice that by its bi-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              property the Poisson bracket on a polynomial Poisson algebra is fixed by its restriction to linear elements
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{-,-\} \;\colon\; V \otimes V \longrightarrow Sym(V)
                    \\,.
          #UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraOfPolynomialPoissonAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (universal enveloping algebra of polynomial Poisson algebra)
            %p
              Given a polynomial Poisson algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sym(V), \{-,-\})
              (def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynomialPoissonAlgebra"}
              %em universal enveloping algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}(V,\{-,-\})
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} associative algebra
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+algebra"} tensor algebra
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} formal variable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℏ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
              adjoined by the two-sided ideal which is generated by the the
              = succeed "-Poisson" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℏ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{U}(V,\{-,-\})
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    T(V)/( x \otimes y - y \otimes x - \hbar \{x,y\} \vert x,y \in V )
                    \\,.
            %p This comes with the quotient projection linear map which we denote by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\rho \;\colon\; T(V)[ [ \hbar ] ] \longrightarrow \mathcal{U}(V,\hbar\{-,-\})
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#PenkavaVanhaecke00"}> Penkava-Vanhaecke 00, def. 3.1
            )
          %p
            The combined linear projection maps from def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynomialPoissonAlgebra"}
            and def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraOfPolynomialPoissonAlgebra"}
            we denote by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi τ
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi ρ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℏ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Sym
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi ℏ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi 𝒰
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tau \coloneqq \rho \circ (\sigma/[ [ \hbar ] ]) \;\colon\; Sym(V)[ [ \hbar ] ] \longrightarrow \mathcal{U}(V,\{-,-\})
                  \\,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          #PolynomialLiePoissonStructure.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structure"} Lie-Poisson structure
                on affine algebraic variety)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n), \pi)
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poisson+manifold"} Poisson manifold
              whose underlying manifold is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi π
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ( C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n, \cdot), \pi^{i j} \partial_i(-) \cdot \partial_j(-)  )
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+functions"} polynomial functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}[x^1, \cdots, x^n ] \hookrightarrow C^\infty(\mathbb{R}^n)
              is a polynomial Poisson algebra according to def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynomialPoissonAlgebra"}
            %p
              In particular if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}, [-,-])
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}^\ast, \{-,-\})
              the corresponding
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structure"} Lie-Poisson manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sym(\mathfrak{g}), \{-,-\})
              where the restriction of the Poisson bracket to linear polynomial elements coincides with the
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{x,y\} = [x,y]
                    \\,.
          #UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraOfLieAlgebra.num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+enveloping+algebra"} universal enveloping algebra
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %p
              In the case of a polynomial
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structure"} Lie-Poisson structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sym(\mathfrak{g}), [-,-])
              (example
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynomialLiePoissonStructure"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}(\mathfrak{g},[-,-])
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraOfPolynomialPoissonAlgebra"}
              (for
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar = 1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+enveloping+algebra"} universal enveloping algebra
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}, [-,-])
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#formal_deformation_quantization_via_universal_enveloping_algebra Formal deformation quantization via universal enveloping algebra
          #UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraProvidesDeformationQuantizationAtLeastToOrder3.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (universal enveloping algebra provides
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
                at least up to order 3)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ( Sym(V), \{-,-\} )
              be a polynomial Poisson algebra (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynomialPoissonAlgebra"}
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraOfPolynomialPoissonAlgebra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+function"} injective
              up to order
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}\cup \{\infty\}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\tau/(\hbar^{n+1}) \;\colon\; Sym(V)[ [ \hbar ] ]/(\hbar^{n+1}) \hookrightarrow \mathcal{U}(V,\hbar\{-,-\})/(\hbar^{n+1})
                    \\,.
            %p
              Then the restriction of the product on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒰
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{U}(V,\hbar\{-,-\})/(\hbar^{n+1})
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℏ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sym(V)/(\hbar^{n+1})
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sym
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sym(V), \{-,-\})
              to order
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              (hence a genuine deformation quantization in the case that
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = \infty
            %p
              Moreover, this is
              %em always
              the case for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℏ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#PenkavaVanhaecke00"}> Penkava-Vanhaecke 00, theorem 3.2 with section 2
            )
          #DeformationQuantizationOfLiePoissonStructuresByUniversalEnvelopingAlgebras.num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+deformation+quantization"} formal deformation quantization
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structures"} Lie-Poisson structures
                by universal enveloping algebras)
            %p
              In the following cases the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi τ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau
              in prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraProvidesDeformationQuantizationAtLeastToOrder3"}
              is injective to arbitrary order, hence in these cases the universal enveloping algebra provides a genuine
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+quantization"} deformation quantization
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the case that the Poisson bracket is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+Poisson+structure"} linear
                  in that restricts as
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi V
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Sym
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\{-,-\} \;\colon\; V \otimes V \longrightarrow V \hookrightarrow Sym(V)
                        \\,.
                %p
                  This is the case of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie-Poisson+structure"} Lie-Poisson structure
                  from example
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PolynomialLiePoissonStructure"}
                  and the universal enveloping algebra that provides it deformation quantization is the standard one (example
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#UniversalEnvelopingAlgebraOfLieAlgebra"}
              %li
                %p more generally, the case that the Poisson bracket restricted to linear elements has linear and constant contribution in that it restricts as
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi V
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi V
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Sym
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\{-,-\} \;\colon\; V \otimes V \longrightarrow \mathbb{R} \oplus V \hookrightarrow Sym(V)
                        \\,.
                %p
                  This includes notably the Poisson structures induced by
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+vector+spaces"} symplectic vector spaces
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo ⊕
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\{-,-\} \;\colon\; (\mathbb{R} \oplus V) \otimes (\mathbb{R} \oplus V) \longrightarrow (\mathbb{R} \oplus V)
                %p
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
                  of the associated
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heisenberg+Lie+algebra"} Heisenberg Lie algebra
          %p
            This is (
            %a{:href => "#PenkavaVanhaecke00"}> Penkava-Vanhaecke 00, p. 26
            ) The first statement in itself is a classical fact (reviewed e.g. in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Gutt11"} Gutt 11
